*** PATCH TARGET ***
Original/PWA/warehouse/picker.html

*** ROOT CAUSE ***
After cancel-picking succeeds, renderPendingTab() replaces #mainContent with a skeleton while asynchronously rebuilding the pending list. The same page contains code paths that directly execute byId('searchDropdown').classList without verifying that the transient DOM node still exists. This creates a client-side race and produces: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'classList').

*** SURGICAL FIX ***
1. In renderPendingTab(), cancel any pending search debounce before replacing the DOM:

    renderPendingTab: function(){
        var self = this;
        if(this.searchTimer){ clearTimeout(this.searchTimer); this.searchTimer = null; }
        safeHTML(byId('mainContent'),
            '<div class="mb-6"><div class="skeleton h-14 w-full mb-4"></div><div class="skeleton h-32 w-full mb-3"></div></div>'
        );

2. In onSearchInput(), guard the dynamically created dropdown:

    onSearchInput: function(query){
        var self = this;
        if(this.searchTimer) clearTimeout(this.searchTimer);
        var dropdown = byId('searchDropdown');
        if(!query || query.trim().length < 1){
            if(dropdown) dropdown.classList.add('hidden');
            return;
        }
        this.searchTimer = setTimeout(function(){
            supabase.from('runsheets').select('runsheet_code, status, run_date, picker_id, run_sheet_details(count)').ilike('runsheet_code', '%' + query.trim() + '%').limit(10).then(function(res){
                self.searchResults = res.data || []; self.renderSearchDropdown();
            });
        }, 300);
    },

3. In openRunsheet(), guard the same dynamically created dropdown:

    openRunsheet: function(code){
        var self = this;
        var dropdown = byId('searchDropdown');
        if(dropdown) dropdown.classList.add('hidden');
        safeHTML(byId('mainContent'), '<div class="text-center py-20"><div class="skeleton h-48 w-full mb-4"></div></div>');
        ...

4. In cancelPicking() success path, clear any stale search debounce before rendering the pending tab:

    if(json && json.success){
        toast('تم إلغاء التحضير', 'success');
        db.session.clear();
        self.session = null;
        if(self.timerInterval) clearInterval(self.timerInterval);
        if(self.searchTimer) { clearTimeout(self.searchTimer); self.searchTimer = null; }
        self.renderPendingTab();
    }

*** NON-CHANGES ***
- Do not change the HTTP invocation in picker.html.
- Do not change start-picking/cancel-picking API contracts.
- Do not change runsheet state logic.
- Do not change stock or allocated_qty logic.
- Do not modify the Golden/Diamond UI beyond these DOM-lifecycle guards.

*** VERIFICATION CONTRACT ***
The cancellation flow must execute:
Picker UI -> cancel-picking HTTP -> DB cancellation -> renderPendingTab -> asynchronous list rebuild
without any direct classList access on a missing #searchDropdown node.
